    </p>
    
    <p class="abstract mathjax">
      <span class="has-text-black-bis has-text-weight-semibold">Abstract</span>:
      <span class="abstract-short has-text-grey-dark mathjax" id="2507.11183v1-abstract-short" style="display: inline;">
        Federated learning is a machine learning approach that enables multiple devices (i.e., <span class="search-hit mathjax">agents</span>) to train a shared model cooperatively without exchanging raw data. This technique keeps&hellip;
        <a class="is-size-7" style="white-space: nowrap;" onclick="document.getElementById('2507.11183v1-abstract-full').style.display = 'inline'; document.getElementById('2507.11183v1-abstract-short').style.display = 'none';">&#9661; More</a>
      </span>
      <span class="abstract-full has-text-grey-dark mathjax" id="2507.11183v1-abstract-full" style="display: none;">
        Federated learning is a machine learning approach that enables multiple devices (i.e., <span class="search-hit mathjax">agents</span>) to train a shared model cooperatively without exchanging raw data. This technique keeps <span class="search-hit mathjax">data</span> <span class="search-hit mathjax">localized</span> on user devices, ensuring <span class="search-hit mathjax">privacy</span> and security, while each <span class="search-hit mathjax">agent</span> trains the model on their own data and only shares model updates. The communication overhead is a significant challenge due to the frequent exchange of model updates between the <span class="search-hit mathjax">agents</span> and the central server. In this paper, we propose a communication-efficient federated learning scheme that utilizes low-rank approximation of neural network gradients and quantization to significantly reduce the network load of the decentralized learning process with minimal impact on the model&#39;s accuracy.
        <a class="is-size-7" style="white-space: nowrap;" onclick="document.getElementById('2507.11183v1-abstract-full').style.display = 'none'; document.getElementById('2507.11183v1-abstract-short').style.display = 'inline';">&#9651; Less</a>
      </span>
    </p>
    

